+// The direct tier computes the common case in WASM and must leave exactly the
+// state the interpreter leaves. Results that are zero or normal (single range
+// for single-precision ops) are computed bit-exactly here, FPSCR included
+// (FPRF, and FI/FR/XX where the interpreter sets them). Anything else (NaN,
+// infinity, denormal, a denormal frC, FE0/FE1 set) re-executes the
+// instruction through the interpreter helper before anything is written, so
+// NaN propagation, VE/ZE suppression, NI flushing and sticky exception bits
+// stay the interpreter's. FMA-family ops always take the helper: the
+// interpreter rounds them once (std::fma plus its single-precision tie fix),
+// which plain WASM arithmetic cannot reproduce.
